---
import CompareLayout from "../../layouts/CompareLayout.astro";
import { whoCanEdit } from "../../data/demo-answers.ts";
import { SFI, VERIFIED } from "../../data/compare.ts";
---

<CompareLayout
  name="Metazoa Snapshot"
  title="sf-intelligence vs Metazoa Snapshot Compared"
  description="Metazoa Snapshot is a paid desktop suite that changes orgs: deploys, data moves, profile cleanups. sf-intelligence is free and only reads. Compare the two."
  path="/compare/metazoa"
  heading="sf-intelligence vs Metazoa Snapshot"
  lede="Both run on your own computer, so “your metadata stays local” is true of each. The real difference is the verb: Snapshot changes orgs, sf-intelligence only explains them."
  short="Metazoa Snapshot is a commercial desktop application, paired with a package installed in the org, that deploys, migrates data, cleans up profiles and ships a library of reports. Pricing is by request. sf-intelligence is free, installs nothing in the org and has no way to write to it. Plan a change with sf-intelligence; make it with a tool built to make changes."
  rows={[
    { label: "What it is", sfi: SFI.what, them: "An org-management suite: deployments, data migration, permission cleanups, reports and diagrams" },
    { label: "Where it runs", sfi: SFI.where, them: "A desktop app that, in Metazoa’s words, “communicates from your personal computer to your Salesforce org”" },
    { label: "Installed in the org", sfi: "Nothing. One read-only retrieve", them: "A managed package from AppExchange, alongside the desktop app" },
    { label: "Writes to the org", sfi: SFI.writes, them: "Yes. Deploying and changing orgs is the core of the product" },
    { label: "Price", sfi: SFI.price, them: "Not published. Metazoa offers “Request Pricing” and a free technical-debt assessment" },
    { label: "AI assistant", sfi: "Works in the assistant you already use, over MCP", them: "Its own Intelligent Assistant, which Metazoa says can “take action” in an org" },
    { label: "Source code", sfi: SFI.source, them: "Closed" },
  ]}
  chooseSfi={[
    "To <strong>spend nothing</strong> and read the code that produces each answer",
    "To <strong>install nothing</strong> in the Salesforce org",
    "Answers in <strong>any MCP assistant</strong>: Claude, Cursor, VS Code + Copilot, Codex",
    "To give an AI agent a tool that <strong>can’t change production</strong>",
  ]}
  chooseThem={[
    "To <strong>deploy</strong> from sandbox to production, with scheduling and rollback",
    "To move data, seed sandboxes, or split and merge orgs",
    "To <strong>change permissions in bulk</strong>, not just read about them",
    "A desktop interface, a catalogue of ready-made reports, and vendor support",
  ]}
  notSfi={[
    "You need to make the change, not plan it. No deploy, migration or bulk edit, ever",
    "You want a desktop app or ready-made reports to click through. It answers in your assistant",
    "You need a vendor on the hook for support and training",
  ]}
  example={whoCanEdit}
  exampleIntro="A permissions question asked of Verdant, the demo org: the reading half of a profile cleanup."
  sources={[
    { label: "metazoa.com home page", href: "https://www.metazoa.com/" },
  ]}
  verified={VERIFIED}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: "Isn’t Metazoa also local and private?",
      a: "Yes. Snapshot runs on your computer too, so keeping metadata off third-party servers isn’t unique to sf-intelligence. The differences are price, read-only versus write-capable, and whether anything is installed in the org.",
    },
    {
      q: "Can sf-intelligence clean up profiles like Snapshot does?",
      a: "It can tell you who can see or edit what, and through which profile or permission set. It can’t change any of it. Use it to plan the cleanup, then make the change in Salesforce or a tool built for deployments.",
    },
    {
      q: "How much does Metazoa Snapshot cost?",
      a: "Metazoa doesn’t publish prices on its site; it asks you to request pricing. sf-intelligence is free.",
    },
  ]}
  related={[{ href: "/use-cases/sharing-troubleshooting", label: "Sharing and permission troubleshooting" }]}
>
  <h2>Why read-only matters here</h2>
  <p>A tool that can deploy has to ask before it does anything risky, and someone has to trust that it asks. sf-intelligence has no deploy, update or delete code at all, so the worst a bad answer can do is be wrong. When you are getting an AI agent approved by security, “it can’t write” is a shorter review than “it can write, but it asks first”.</p>
  <p>It also means the two aren’t really substitutes. sf-intelligence won’t refactor two hundred profiles for you; Snapshot isn’t free. A sensible split is to ask sf-intelligence what a change touches, then make the change with the tool you use for releases.</p>
</CompareLayout>
